From: lws-hmi <lws-hmi@local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: skip init without display-subsystem (QEMU virt)

The shared product-line Image also boots under QEMU (-machine virt) for
P3.2. rockchip_drm_init always calls rockchip_gem_get_ddr_info() → SIP
SMC into ATF. On virt there is no EL3/ATF, so the SMC is an undefined
instruction and kills kernel_init ("Attempted to kill init").

Skip the whole Rockchip DRM bring-up when DT has no
rockchip,display-subsystem (device always has it; QEMU dummy-virt does
not). Emulator display is virtio-gpu.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_drv.c
@@ -2567,10 +2567,22 @@ static int __init rockchip_drm_init(void)
 {
 	int ret;
 
 	if (drm_firmware_drivers_only())
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	/* Same Image on QEMU virt: no Rockchip display DT → no ATF SIP. */
+	{
+		struct device_node *np;
+
+		np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "rockchip,display-subsystem");
+		if (!np) {
+			pr_info("rockchip-drm: no display-subsystem, skip (non-Rockchip DT)\n");
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
+		of_node_put(np);
+	}
+
 	num_rockchip_sub_drivers = 0;
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP_VVOP)
 	ADD_ROCKCHIP_SUB_DRIVER(vvop_platform_driver, CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP_VVOP);
 #else
 	ADD_ROCKCHIP_SUB_DRIVER(vop_platform_driver, CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_VOP);
